al\">B</mi><mo>&#8746;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>85</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>95</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math>&nbsp;lies in the interval :"}, "options": [{"id": "dc75d1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>36</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925adf7"}, {"id": "1bc700", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>35</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925adf8"}, {"id": "969709", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925adf9"}, {"id": "846fc5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925adfa"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925adfb", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4553"], "concepts": ["60e2faab66f9ce3f243b4519"], "question": {"text": "If an unbiased die, marked with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;on its faces is thrown five times, then the probability that the product of the outcomes is positive, is :"}, "options": [{"id": "d02a2f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>881</mn><mn>2592</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925adfc"}, {"id": "719d9b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>521</mn><mn>2592</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925adfd"}, {"id": "fa9619", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>440</mn><mn>2592</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925adfe"}, {"id": "fd5c0f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>27</mn><mn>288</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925adff"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae00", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3d66f9ce3f243b4d71"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d54"], "question": {"text": "A fair die is thrown until <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> appears. Then the probability, that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> appears in even number of throws, is"}, "options": [{"id": "66ff11", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae01"}, {"id": "0798a9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae02"}, {"id": "74e7ed", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae03"}, {"id": "190255", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae04"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae05", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1ebd"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e88"], "question": {"text": "The minimum number of times one has to toss a fair coin so that the probability of observing at least one head is at least <math><mn>90</mn><mi>%</mi></math> is:"}, "options": [{"id": "864e5f", "text": "<math><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae06"}, {"id": "04370f", "text": "<math><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae07"}, {"id": "5ca63b", "text": "<math><mn>5</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae08"}, {"id": "c0d97c", "text": "<math><mn>3</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae09"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae0a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fafb66f9ce3f243b498a"], "concepts": ["60e2fafb66f9ce3f243b4967"], "question": {"text": "Two balls are selected at random one by one without replacement from a bag containing 4 white and 6 black balls. If the probability that the first selected ball is black, given that the second selected ball is also black, is $\\frac{m}{n}$, where $\\operatorname{gcd}(m, n)=1$, then $m+n$ is equal to :"}, "options": [{"id": "8157aa", "text": "$4$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae0b"}, {"id": "a84514", "text": "$14$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae0c"}, {"id": "82a9dd", "text": "$13$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae0d"}, {"id": "c3eff9", "text": "$11$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae0e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae0f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["6117af49c5f0702080bdda21"], "concepts": ["6117af48c5f0702080bdd9b5"], "question": {"text": "<p>A random variable <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> has the following probability distribution:</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>X</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>k</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi>k</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mi>k</mi></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>is equal to</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "978285", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae10"}, {"id": "273afd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae11"}, {"id": "30494d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae12"}, {"id": "e88ff0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae13"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae14", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8f"], "concepts": ["6176f3e76581241c70729fbf"], "question": {"text": "If a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;lies in the region bounded by the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-axis, straight lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></math>, then the probability that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;is"}, "options": [{"id": "bbad3c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae15"}, {"id": "b807dd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae16"}, {"id": "2869db", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae17"}, {"id": "260ca9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae18"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae19", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["69464f174ddd12548dbf2f8b"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d54"], "question": {"text": "Let <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> be two independent events such that <math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> and <math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math> Then, which of the following is true?"}, "options": [{"id": "061c5a", "text": "<math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae1a"}, {"id": "f69977", "text": "<math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>'</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae1b"}, {"id": "728ee0", "text": "<math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>'</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>'</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae1c"}, {"id": "b0e36a", "text": "<math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∪</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae1d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae1e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["6117b03dc5f0702080bdea7d"], "question": {"text": "Two dices are rolled. If both dices have six faces numbered <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>7</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then the probability that the sum of the numbers on the top faces is less than or equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math> is:"}, "options": [{"id": "f23d99", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae1f"}, {"id": "a36cf1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>17</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae20"}, {"id": "f589d0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae21"}, {"id": "e22de0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae22"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae23", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4553"], "concepts": ["60e2faab66f9ce3f243b450c"], "question": {"text": "Given three indentical bags each containing 10 balls, whose colours are as follows :<br/>$\\begin{array}{cccc} & \\text{Red} & \\text{Blue} & \\text{Green} \\\\ \\text{Bag I} & 3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ \\text{Bag II} & 4 & 3 & 3 \\\\ \\text{Bag III} & 5 & 1 & 4\\end{array}$<br/>A person chooses a bag at random and takes out a ball. If the ball is Red, the probability that it is from bag I is p and if the balls is Green, the probability that it is from bag III is q , then the value of $\\left(\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{p}}+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{q}}\\right)$ is :"}, "options": [{"id": "554561", "text": "$6$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae24"}, {"id": "7a85bd", "text": "$9$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae25"}, {"id": "96761c", "text": "$7$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae26"}, {"id": "c718f9", "text": "$8$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae27"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae28", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["6117af49c5f0702080bdda21"], "concepts": ["6117afaec5f0702080bde0f1"], "question": {"text": "<p>The random variable&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>&nbsp;follows binomial distribution <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, for which the difference of the mean and the variance is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>.</p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math> is equal to</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "aed9bd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae29"}, {"id": "8e6185", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae2a"}, {"id": "783444", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae2b"}, {"id": "6791c8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae2c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae2d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b454e"], "concepts": ["60e5671b499d1e49588f87f8"], "question": {"text": "Let the sum of two positive integers be 24 . If the probability, that their product is not less than $\\frac{3}{4}$ times their greatest possible product, is $\\frac{m}{n}$, where $\\operatorname{gcd}(m, n)=1$, then $n-m$ equals"}, "options": [{"id": "a6b5cd", "text": "10", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae2e"}, {"id": "533671", "text": "9", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae2f"}, {"id": "5e22e0", "text": "11", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae30"}, {"id": "81dc8a", "text": "8", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae31"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae32", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1ebd"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e88"], "question": {"text": "An unbiased coin is tossed. If the outcome is a head then a pair of unbiased dice is rolled and the sum of the numbers obtained on them is noted. If the toss of the coin results in tail then a card from a well-shuffled pack of nine cards numbered <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1,</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>9</mn></math> is randomly picked and the number on the card is noted. The probability that the noted number is either <math><mn>7</mn></math> or <math><mn>8</mn></math> is"}, "options": [{"id": "e00053", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>13</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>36</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae33"}, {"id": "66397f", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>19</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>72</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae34"}, {"id": "070054", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>72</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae35"}, {"id": "b8349d", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>19</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>36</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae36"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae37", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fafb66f9ce3f243b498a"], "concepts": ["60e2fafb66f9ce3f243b4967"], "question": {"text": "In a bolt factory, machines&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;manufacture respectively&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;of the total bolts.&nbsp;Of their output&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;percent are respectively defective bolts. A bolt is drawn at random from the product. If the bolt drawn is found the defective then the probability that it is manufactured by the machine&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;"}, "options": [{"id": "b9672d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>14</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae38"}, {"id": "22a8a4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>28</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae39"}, {"id": "870f49", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae3a"}, {"id": "6f5d9e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae3b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae3c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3d66f9ce3f243b4d71"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d54"], "question": {"text": "In a workshop, there are five machines and the probability of any one of them to be out of service on a day is <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> . If the probability that at most two machines will be out of service on the same day is <math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo></math> then <math><mi>k</mi></math> is equal to"}, "options": [{"id": "43b27a", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>17</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae3d"}, {"id": "9ca25a", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>17</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae3e"}, {"id": "c1278f", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>17</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae3f"}, {"id": "303b08", "text": "<math><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae40"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae41", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b454e"], "concepts": ["60e2faab66f9ce3f243b4507"], "question": {"text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;be three mutually exclusive events such that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>p</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. If the maximum and minimum values of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math>&nbsp;are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to:"}, "options": [{"id": "7d4453", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae42"}, {"id": "ae34ce", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae43"}, {"id": "5e33ff", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae44"}, {"id": "0fc3c9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae45"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae46", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["6117af49c5f0702080bdda21"], "concepts": ["6117b07bc5f0702080bdef7b"], "question": {"text": "In a game, a man wins Rs. <math><mn>100</mn></math> if he gets <math><mn>5</mn></math> or <math><mn>6</mn></math> on a throw of a fair die and loses Rs. <math><mn>50</mn></math> for getting any other number on the die. If he decides to throw the die either till he gets a five or a six or to a maximum of three throws, then his expected gain/loss (in rupees) is :"}, "options": [{"id": "10283c", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>400</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>  gain", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae47"}, {"id": "12a657", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>400</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>  gain", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae48"}, {"id": "9a8846", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>400</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>  loss", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae49"}, {"id": "bc2905", "text": "<math><mn>0</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae4a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae4b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "If an unbiased dice is rolled thrice, then the probability of getting a greater number in the $i^{\\text {th }}$ roll than the number obtained in the $(i-1)^{\\text {th }}$ roll, $i=2,3$, is equal to"}, "options": [{"id": "32395a", "text": "$3 / 54$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae4c"}, {"id": "f7cf63", "text": "$2 / 54$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae4d"}, {"id": "094af2", "text": "$1 / 54$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae4e"}, {"id": "90b0d2", "text": "$5 / 54$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae4f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae50", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4553"], "concepts": ["60e2faab66f9ce3f243b450c"], "question": {"text": "A fair die is tossed until six is obtained on it. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>&nbsp;be the number of required tosses, then the conditional probability <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>&#10878;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#8739;</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math> is :"}, "options": [{"id": "ddc023", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae51"}, {"id": "e994a2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae52"}, {"id": "bacdcc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae53"}, {"id": "19c462", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>125</mn><mn>216</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925ae54"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:20.783Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:20.783Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afd9"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afd7", "title": "Mathematics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d92", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afbb", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4553"], "concepts": ["60e2faab66f9ce3f243b450c"], "question": {"text": "A card from a pack of 52 cards is lost. From the remaining 51 cards, $n$ cards are drawn and are found to be spades. If the probability of the lost card to be a spade is $\\frac{11}{50}$, the n is equal to"}, "options": [{"id": "11a444", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afbc"}, {"id": "b5f86e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afbd"}, {"id": "8ae3af", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afbe"}, {"id": "d2c937", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afbf"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afc0", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3d66f9ce3f243b4d71"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d54"], "question": {"text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> be three independent events in a sample space. The probability that only <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> occur is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;only <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> occurs is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math> and only <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> occurs is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math> be the probability that none of the events <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math> occurs and these <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> probabilities satisfy the equations <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#946;</mi><mi>&#947;</mi></math> (All the probabilities are assumed to lie in the interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfenced></math> Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math> is equal to______."}, "options": [{"id": "839ca1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afc1"}, {"id": "1f2703", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afc2"}, {"id": "a559ba", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afc3"}, {"id": "f81d23", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afc4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afc5", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e40fd6f1ef260f84ed1ebd"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e88"], "question": {"text": "The probability of a man hitting a target is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math> The least number of shots required, so that the&nbsp;probability of his hitting the target at least once is greater than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math> is...."}, "options": [{"id": "15245b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afc6"}, {"id": "0bee3c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afc7"}, {"id": "ac5b71", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afc8"}, {"id": "8e1463", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afc9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afca", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fafb66f9ce3f243b498a"], "concepts": ["60e2fafb66f9ce3f243b4967"], "question": {"text": "The urns&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;contains&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;red,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;black;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;red,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;black and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi></math>&nbsp;red,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;black balls respectively. One of the urns is selected at random and a ball is drawn. If the ball drawn is red and the&nbsp;probability that it is drawn from urn&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, then the square of length of the side of largest equilateral triangle, inscribed in the parabola&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;with one vertex at vertex of parabola is"}, "options": [{"id": "04a0a9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afcb"}, {"id": "e9799f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afcc"}, {"id": "d92ae4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afcd"}, {"id": "857737", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afce"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afcf", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["6117af49c5f0702080bdda21"], "concepts": ["6117afaec5f0702080bde0f1"], "question": {"text": "Three balls are drawn at random from a bag containing 5 blue and 4 yellow balls. Let the random variables $X$ and $Y$ respectively denote the number of blue and yellow balls. If $\\bar{X}$ and $\\bar{Y}$ are the means of $X$ and $Y$ respectively, then $7 \\bar{X}+4 \\bar{Y}$ is equal to________"}, "options": [{"id": "b92796", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afd0"}, {"id": "2f08fd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afd1"}, {"id": "efe21b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afd2"}, {"id": "a24e4a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afd3"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 5, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:20.882Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:20.882Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 1, "_id": "69de4f402ee0e063d925afda"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures": [], "tags": [], "timeRestrictionSlots": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T11:16:13.413Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-17T04:58:06.882Z", "testType": "PYQs as Chapter Tests", "isResumeBufferAllowed": true, "enableAccessibility": true, "maxA